{"assets":["/statement-assets/6099c970cfc70c36c43f303127af7aefd20e49dec7583a5fab7b464cdd27353a.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"660","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Bear and Bowling 4"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Limak is an old brown bear. He often goes bowling with his friends. Today he feels really good and tries to beat his own record!"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For rolling a ball one gets a score — an integer (maybe negative) number of points. Score for the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th roll is multiplied by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" and scores are summed up. So, for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" rolls with scores "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s1, s2, ..., sk"},{"kind":"text","text":", the total score is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/6099c970cfc70c36c43f303127af7aefd20e49dec7583a5fab7b464cdd27353a.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". The total score is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":" if there were no rolls."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Limak made "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" rolls and got score "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" for the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of them. He wants to maximize his total score and he came up with an interesting idea. He can say that some first rolls were only a warm-up, and that he wasn't focused during the last rolls. More formally, he can cancel any prefix and any suffix of the sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., an"},{"kind":"text","text":". It is allowed to cancel all rolls, or to cancel none of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The total score is calculated as if there were only non-canceled rolls. So, the first non-canceled roll has score multiplied by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":", the second one has score multiplied by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":", and so on, till the last non-canceled roll."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"What maximum total score can Limak get?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 2·105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the total number of rolls made by Limak."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., an"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"|ai| ≤ 107)"},{"kind":"text","text":" — scores for Limak's rolls."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the maximum possible total score after cancelling rolls."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6\n5 -1000 1 -3 7 -8\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"16\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n1000 1000 1001 1000 1000\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"15003\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n-60 -70 -80\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample test, Limak should cancel the first two rolls, and one last roll. He will be left with rolls "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1,  - 3, 7"},{"kind":"text","text":" what gives him the total score "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1·1 + 2·( - 3) + 3·7 = 1 - 6 + 21 = 16"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"660F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/660/problem/F"}